Kind: ablation
Issue: #780
Takes out: the three tails' fresh start -- thread_exception_return, thread_bootstrap_return and restart_mach_syscall no longer put %rsp back at kernel_stack, so every exception act_test's arm seventeen answers with "resume" would come back through the tail one level deeper on the kernel stack, a hundred times; the shared tail's check (5f875988) says so the first time a tail comes into it off the top.
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 4
Expect: trap: a return to ring 3 came into the shared tail with %rsp 0x[0-9a-f]+, not at the top of its kernel stack
Note: both accelerators: the check is the kernel's, not the processor's.  Before the check, a kept stack showed only where its overflow hit something, which nothing guards: on victus (AMD), 4 of 4, a double fault under KVM and a kernel page fault under TCG; on OMEGA (Intel, 30/10), nothing at all under KVM, and under TCG a single-step trap at an address in data, through a frame the overflow had written.

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/trap/entry.S b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/trap/entry.S
index da11f10c..4d0f9b20 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/trap/entry.S
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/trap/entry.S
@@ -610,7 +610,6 @@ isr_table:
  * thread to resume there.
  */
 thread_exception_return:
-	movq	%gs:PERCPU_KERNEL_STACK, %rsp	/* nothing below is live (#780) */
 	xorl	%ebp, %ebp			/* and no frame above it */
 	callq	thread_return_ast	/* AST_APC first: see trap.c */
 	jmp	thread_user_frame_return
@@ -624,7 +623,6 @@ thread_exception_return:
  * prepared by thread_set_state(), and resuming it is resuming it.
  */
 thread_bootstrap_return:
-	movq	%gs:PERCPU_KERNEL_STACK, %rsp	/* nothing below is live (#780) */
 	xorl	%ebp, %ebp			/* and no frame above it */
 	callq	thread_return_ast	/* AST_APC first: see trap.c */
 	jmp	thread_user_frame_return
@@ -643,7 +641,6 @@ thread_bootstrap_return:
  * have to rewind rip by the instruction's two bytes first (#780).
  */
 restart_mach_syscall:
-	movq	%gs:PERCPU_KERNEL_STACK, %rsp	/* nothing below is live (#780) */
 	xorl	%ebp, %ebp			/* and no frame above it */
 	callq	thread_return_ast	/* AST_APC first: see trap.c */
 	jmp	thread_user_frame_return
